INSERT INTO `quiz_questions` VALUES (50,2,'What does Backpropagation compute in a neural network?','Gradients of the loss function with respect to weights using chain rule','Accuracy of the model','Dataset normalization parameters','Batch size for training','A','Medium',0),(53,26,'What is the primary optimization objective when implementing something in Module 1: Advanced Deep Learning & Transformers?','Minimize execution latency and algorithmic complexity','Increase memory overhead for caching','Force synchronous single-threaded bottlenecks','Disable thread safety invariants','A','Medium',0),(54,26,'In production deployments of something, which architectural pattern ensures fault tolerance?','Circuit Breaker with Graceful Degradation','Monolithic Shared-State Single Points of Failure','Unbounded Recursive Polling Loops','Hardcoded Plaintext Environment Secrets','A','Medium',0),(55,26,'When evaluating performance tradeoffs in something ( Level), what is the primary risk?','Memory leaks due to uncollected cyclic references','Over-indexed B-Tree storage overhead','Sub-millisecond query response latency','Deterministic hash collision minimization','A','Medium',0),(56,26,'Which diagnostic metric provides the most actionable telemetry for something health?','P99 Response Time & Error Rate Gradient','Raw Line Count of Source Code','Color Scheme Palette Contrast Ratio','Local Git Commit Timestamp Frequency','A','Medium',0),(72,31,'Which queue has higher priority than the macrotask callback queue?','Microtask Queue','Timer Queue','I/O Polling Queue','Check Queue','a','medium',1),(73,32,'Knowledge check on helo0','Architecture Layer A','Architecture Layer B','Core Design C','Service Registry D','a','medium',1),(74,34,'Which Dockerfile instruction specifies the base image to build upon?','FROM','BASE','IMAGE','ROOT','a','medium',1),(76,35,'Which Dockerfile instruction specifies the base image to build upon?','FROM','BASE','IMAGE','ROOT','a','medium',1),(78,36,'In the context of sending emails from a Java backend via SMTP, what is the primary purpose of the HELO command?','To authenticate the user with a username and password.','To identify the sending client\'s domain name to the SMTP server.','To specify the recipient\'s email address.','To initiate a secure TLS/SSL encrypted session.','b','medium',1),(79,36,'When configuring a modern Java Spring Boot application to send emails via a cloud SMTP relay, why is EHLO preferred over the older HELO command?','EHLO supports Extended SMTP (ESMTP) features like authentication and TLS encryption.','EHLO is a proprietary command exclusive to AWS SES and Google Workspace.','EHLO automatically compresses the email body to save cloud bandwidth.','EHLO bypasses the need for DNS MX record verification.','a','medium',1),(80,36,'Which Jakarta Mail (formerly JavaMail) property is used to explicitly set the domain name sent in the HELO/EHLO command?','mail.smtp.localhost','mail.smtp.helo.name','mail.smtp.domain','mail.smtp.clientname','a','medium',1),(81,36,'During a standard SMTP session initiated by a Java application, when should the client send the HELO or EHLO command?','Immediately after receiving the server\'s initial 220 connection greeting.','Right after sending the MAIL FROM command.','Only after the STARTTLS handshake has fully completed.','Immediately before sending the QUIT command to close the connection.','a','medium',1),(82,36,'Why do cloud email providers (like AWS SES or SendGrid) reject SMTP connections if the domain provided in the HELO/EHLO command is malformed or unresolvable?','To enforce basic spam prevention and verify the sender\'s identity against DNS records.','Because unresolvable domains cause physical memory leaks on cloud mail servers.','To force the Java client to use HTTP-based REST APIs instead of SMTP.','Because the SMTP protocol requires the HELO domain to match the recipient\'s domain.','a','medium',1),(83,37,'Which Kafka parameter controls minimum in-sync replicas for write acknowledgment?','min.insync.replicas','acks=all','replication.factor','cleanup.policy','a','medium',1),(84,38,'In a custom Spring Boot starter, how does the @ConditionalOnMissingBean annotation behave when registering a bean?','It registers the bean only if no other bean of the same type or name is already defined in the application context.','It registers the bean only if the target class is completely missing from the classpath at runtime.','It overrides any user-defined beans of the same type to guarantee that starter defaults are strictly enforced.','It throws a BeanCreationException during startup if another bean of the same type is detected.','a','medium',1),(85,38,'When using @WebMvcTest(MyController.class) to test a Spring Boot controller, which of the following components is automatically scanned and loaded into the ApplicationContext?','Only Spring MVC infrastructure, @Controller, @ControllerAdvice, and WebMvcConfigurer beans.','The entire application context including @Service, @Repository, and @Component beans.','Only @Repository beans and the database connection pool configuration.','No beans are loaded; it only starts an embedded Servlet container like Tomcat on a random port.','a','medium',1),(86,38,'If a configuration property \'app.timeout\' is defined in multiple places, which of the following sources has the highest precedence according to Spring Boot\'s default externalized configuration order?','Command-line arguments (e.g., --app.timeout=5000).','Profile-specific application properties packaged inside the jar (e.g., application-dev.properties).','OS Environment variables (e.g., APP_TIMEOUT=5000).','Default properties defined via SpringApplication.setDefaultProperties.','a','medium',1),(87,38,'How does Spring Boot expose Kubernetes Liveness and Readiness probes natively via Actuator?','Through the \'/actuator/health/liveness\' and \'/actuator/health/readiness\' endpoints when running in a Kubernetes environment or when explicitly enabled.','By automatically opening separate ports (8081 and 8082) dedicated solely to Kubernetes probe traffic.','Through a single \'/actuator/k8s\' endpoint that returns a combined JSON status of all probes.','By writing probe status directly to \'/tmp/healthy\' and \'/tmp/ready\' files on the container filesystem.','a','medium',1),(88,38,'When \'server.shutdown=graceful\' is configured in Spring Boot, what is the behavior of the embedded web server during application shutdown?','It stops accepting new requests but allows active requests to complete within a configured grace period.','It immediately terminates all active connections and shuts down the JVM to prevent data corruption.','It redirects all incoming traffic to a backup instance configured in the application properties.','It keeps the server running indefinitely until all active HTTP sessions naturally expire.','a','medium',1),(89,39,'When dealing with a highly skewed numerical feature containing outliers, which imputation strategy is most robust for preserving the central tendency without introducing significant bias?','Mean imputation','Median imputation','Zero imputation','Mode imputation','b','medium',1),(90,39,'In a binary classification problem with a severe class imbalance (e.g., 99% negative, 1% positive), which metric provides the most reliable assessment of model performance regarding the minority class?','Receiver Operating Characteristic Area Under Curve (ROC-AUC)','Precision-Recall Area Under Curve (PR-AUC)','Accuracy','F1-Score at a default 0.5 threshold','b','medium',1),(91,39,'Before applying Principal Component Analysis (PCA) for dimensionality reduction, why is it critical to standardize features to have a mean of 0 and a standard deviation of 1?','To ensure the principal components are mutually orthogonal','To prevent features with larger scales from dominating the calculation of covariance and eigenvectors','To convert non-linear relationships into linear ones','To guarantee that the resulting principal components follow a normal distribution','b','medium',1),(92,39,'How does severe multicollinearity (high correlation between independent variables) affect the training and interpretability of a Random Forest regressor compared to a Multiple Linear Regression model?','It destabilizes the Random Forest predictions, making them highly sensitive to small changes in training data.','It has little impact on Random Forest predictive performance, but it can dilute the calculated feature importance metrics among the correlated features.','It prevents the Random Forest algorithm from converging during the training phase.','It forces the Random Forest to only select one of the correlated features and completely ignore the others across all trees.','b','medium',1),(93,39,'Why does L1 regularization (Lasso) produce sparse models with coefficients driven exactly to zero, whereas L2 regularization (Ridge) only shrinks coefficients close to zero?','L1 uses a non-differentiable absolute value penalty whose constraint region has sharp corners (vertices) on the axes.','L1 uses a quadratic penalty that penalizes larger coefficients more severely than smaller ones.','L1 optimization is solved using closed-form analytical solutions that force zero values.','L1 regularization increases the bias of the model while L2 regularization only increases the variance.','a','medium',1);
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `quiz_questions` ENABLE KEYS */;
UNLOCK TABLES;

